<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Second Dynasty of Egypt</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Second Dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> ruled from about 2890 to 2686 BCE, the second line of kings of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/early-dynastic-period">Early Dynastic period</a>. Its rulers included Hotepsekhemwy, Nynetjer, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peribsen">Peribsen</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khasekhemwy">Khasekhemwy</a>, and the period seems to have seen internal division before Khasekhemwy reunited the country. It was followed by the Third Dynasty and the Old Kingdom.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/second-dynasty-of-egypt.jpg" alt="Second Dynasty of Egypt" width="320" height="405" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Geni · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Khasekhemwy_statue_Ashmolean.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
